Package: simonnote
Version: 1.0.0-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Simone Company <simone@simonecompany.com>
Installed-Size: 770
Depends: libadwaita-1-0 (>= 1.5~beta), libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), libglib2.0-0t64 (>= 2.76), libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.12.0), libpango-1.0-0 (>= 1.14.0)
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/simonecompany/simonnote
Description: Fast, minimal note-taking app for GNOME
 Simon-Note is a minimal and fast note-taking application written in Rust
 using GTK4 and LibAdwaita. It provides a clean, GNOME-style interface
 with support for editing large text files (20-50 MB) without lag.
 .
 Features:
  * GNOME-style interface with header bar and dark/light theme support
  * UTF-8 text file editing
  * Large files handled with asynchronous I/O and smooth scrolling
  * Keyboard shortcuts for common operations
  * Undo/redo-free minimal interface focused on speed
  * Native GNOME integration with LibAdwaita
